</code></pre> <p>How the panel's effects fit together, in the order they run after a prompt is chosen:</p> <ol> <li><code>selectPrompt</code> sets <code>slug</code> and clears <code>templateId</code>, which triggers two fetches in parallel: <code>usePromptDetail(slug)</code> and <code>useBundledTemplates(slug)</code> (the latter passes <code>prompt_slug</code> so the backend marks the recommended template).</li> <li>When the bundled list arrives, the preselection effect keeps the current template if it is still in the list and otherwise picks the <code>recommended</code> one, falling back to the first. A user's explicit choice therefore survives a refetch, while switching prompts resets to the new recommendation.</li> <li>When the detail arrives, <code>schemaToFields</code> derives the field list and the initialization effect computes values: schema defaults, overlaid once with deep-link values. The <code>appliedDeepLink</code> ref guarantees that URL values are applied to the first prompt only; choosing a different prompt later starts from that prompt's defaults.</li> <li>If the deep-link slug returns 404, the fallback effect hands the slug text back to <code>UploadPage</code>, which switches to the free-text tab.</li> <li>On Generate, the button runs <code>validate</code> (client-side checks plus "a template is selected"), posts, polls and finally calls <code>onNavigate</code>. On Review outline first, the panel renders the prompt on the server (so the outline sees exactly the text the backend validated) and delegates the Redux hand-off to <code>UploadPage</code>.</li> </ol> <p>Values are kept as typed JavaScript values (numbers for integers, the original enum value rather than its string form), because the backend validates with JSON Schema types: sending <code>"37"</code> for an <code>integer</code> field fails with <code>invalid_variables</code> even though it looks right in the form.</p>

