</code></pre> <p><code>{language}</code> is the stored language, or, when empty or <code>auto</code>, the instruction "auto-detect from the slide content and use the same language as the slide content" (<code>generate_slide_content.py:87-100</code>). In the web UI path <code>/prepare</code> clears the language, so this instruction is what slides always see. <code>{slide_number_section}</code> is <code># Slide Number:\n&lt;n&gt;</code> with a one-based number (<code>generate_slide_content.py:152-155</code>), which lets "on slide 5" instructions apply. <code>{content}</code> is the outline Markdown for this slide.</p>

Order <code>type</code> Payload Source 1 <code>chunk</code> <code>"{ \"slides\": [ "</code> (opening text) <code>presentation.py:2360-2363</code> per slide <code>chunk</code> the slide as compact JSON (<code>slide.model_dump_json()</code>) <code>presentation.py:2421-2424</code> interleaved <code>slide_assets</code> <code>{"type": "slide_assets", "slide_index": i, "slide": {...}, "warnings": [...]}</code> <code>presentation.py:2426-2446</code>, <code>presentation.py:2453-2470</code> after last slide <code>chunk</code> <code>" ] }"</code> (closing text) <code>presentation.py:2448-2451</code> remaining <code>slide_assets</code> one per slide whose assets were not yet reported <code>presentation.py:2453-2470</code> last (success) <code>complete</code> <code>{"type": "complete", "presentation": &lt;PresentationWithSlides&gt;}</code> <code>presentation.py:2503-2511</code> last (failure) <code>error</code> <code>{"type": "error", "detail": "..."}</code> <code>presentation.py:2379-2381</code> or <code>safe_sse_stream</code> <p>Exactly one <code>slide_assets</code> frame is sent per slide, either right after a later slide's <code>chunk</code> (if the assets finished while the next LLM call was running) or after the closing chunk. A slide frame looks like this (abridged; field order follows <code>SlideModel</code>, <code>servers/fastapi/models/sql/slide.py:9-30</code>, and <code>owner_id</code> is excluded):</p> <pre><code>event: response
data: {"type": "chunk", "chunk": "{\"id\":\"5c1e...\",\"presentation\":\"8f0c...\",\"layout_group\":\"3b6f...\",\"layout\":\"intro-hero\",\"index\":0,\"content\":{\"hero\":{\"headline\":\"Q3 Business Review\"},\"__speaker_note__\":\"...\"},\"html_content\":null,\"speaker_note\":\"...\",\"properties\":null,\"ui\":{...}}"}

event: response
data: {"type": "slide_assets", "slide_index": 0, "slide": {"id": "5c1e...", "index": 0, "content": {"hero": {"headline": "Q3 Business Review"}, "hero_image": {"image_prompt": "...", "image_url": "/app_data/images/..."}}, "ui": {...}}, "warnings": []}
</code></pre> <p>Warning objects are either image-provider warnings <code>{"status_code": 502, "detail": "...", "code": null}</code> from <code>image_generation_warning</code> (<code>servers/fastapi/utils/image_generation_error.py:75-86</code>) or <code>{"type": "asset_generation_failed", "message": "Some slide assets could not be generated."}</code> when the whole asset task raised (<code>presentation.py:2350-2355</code>).</p> <p>Gotcha</p> <p>The <code>chunk</code> frames concatenate to <code>{ "slides": [ {slide0}{slide1} ] }</code>: there is no comma between slides, so the accumulated text is not valid JSON. The browser copes because it parses each slide chunk on its own and runs <code>jsonrepair</code> over the accumulation (<code>usePresentationStreaming.ts:454-510</code>). If you write a new client, parse each slide chunk individually rather than the concatenation.</p>

