servers/fastapi/services/image_generation_service.py (excerpt)<pre><code>def _closest_ratio_option(
    target_size: tuple[float, float] | None,
    options: tuple[str, ...],
    separator: str,
) -&gt; str | None:
    if target_size is None:
        return None
    target_ratio = target_size[0] / target_size[1]

    def ratio(option: str) -&gt; float:
        width, height = option.split(separator)
        return float(width) / float(height)

    return min(
        options,
        key=lambda option: abs(math.log(target_ratio / ratio(option))),
    )
</code></pre> <p>Comparing ratios in log space makes "twice as wide" and "twice as tall" equally far from square. The option lists are:</p> <ul> <li>OpenAI (<code>GPT_IMAGE_SIZES</code>, <code>servers/fastapi/services/image_generation_service.py:55</code>): <code>1024x1024</code>, <code>1536x1024</code>, <code>1024x1536</code>. Used only when the model name is <code>gpt-image-2</code> or <code>gpt-image-1.5</code>; any other model gets <code>1024x1024</code> (<code>_openai_image_size</code>, <code>servers/fastapi/services/image_generation_service.py:93</code>).</li> <li>Gemini (<code>GEMINI_IMAGE_RATIOS</code>, <code>servers/fastapi/services/image_generation_service.py:56</code>): <code>1:1</code>, <code>2:3</code>, <code>3:2</code>, <code>3:4</code>, <code>4:3</code>, <code>4:5</code>, <code>5:4</code>, <code>9:16</code>, <code>16:9</code>, <code>21:9</code>. With no target size, no <code>image_config</code> is sent and the model picks.</li> <li>ComfyUI: no mapping; the rounded pixel dimensions are written into the workflow (Step 5.4).</li> <li>Open WebUI: always <code>1024x1024</code>, target size ignored (<code>servers/fastapi/services/image_generation_service.py:345</code>).</li> </ul> <p>A worked example: a full-bleed 1280 by 720 box has ratio 1.778. Against <code>1536x1024</code> (ratio 1.5) the distance is <code>|ln(1.778 / 1.5)| = 0.170</code>; against <code>1024x1024</code> it is <code>0.575</code>; against <code>1024x1536</code> it is <code>0.981</code>. The landscape size wins. The unit tests pin a few more cases (<code>servers/fastapi/tests/unit/test_template_image_targets.py:166</code> and <code>servers/fastapi/tests/unit/test_template_image_targets.py:183</code>):</p> Target (w, h) OpenAI size Gemini ratio none <code>1024x1024</code> none (auto) (1600, 900) <code>1536x1024</code> <code>16:9</code> (900, 1600) <code>1024x1536</code> <code>9:16</code> (1200, 1100) <code>1024x1024</code> not tested (1000, 1000) not tested <code>1:1</code> (500, 400) not tested <code>5:4</code> (2100, 900) not tested <code>21:9</code> <p>Note</p> <p>Presenton never resizes or crops the returned image to the slot. A 1024 by 1024 PNG stays 1024 by 1024 on disk (<code>servers/fastapi/tests/unit/test_template_image_targets.py:300</code>). Fitting is done by the renderer; see From template to schema to slide.</p>

