</code></pre> <p>The final options object (<code>scripts/run-presentation-export.mjs:71-80</code>) contains only the keys that have values:</p> Option Meaning (as far as the caller shows) <code>outputDirectory</code> where export-core writes the result <code>tempDirectory</code> scratch space <code>browserLaunchOptions.executablePath</code> the Chromium binary to launch <code>puppeteerCacheDirectory</code> browser cache location <code>urlConfigs</code> a list of <code>{ url, match: "origin", cookies? , headers? }</code> rules; cookies for the page origin, and in Electron a header rule for each app origin <code>modifyWindow</code> a function built with <code>new Function(...)</code> that merges <code>{ NEXT_PUBLIC_FAST_API, ASSETS_BASE_URL }</code> into <code>window.env</code> (<code>scripts/run-presentation-export.mjs:23-35</code>) <p><code>parseCookieHeader()</code> splits on <code>;</code>, keeps everything after the first <code>=</code> as the value, and ignores items without a name (<code>scripts/run-presentation-export.mjs:9-21</code>).</p> <p>Gotcha: <code>ASSETS_BASE_URL</code> is injected but unused by the page</p> <p>FastAPI always sets <code>ASSETS_BASE_URL=/app_data</code> and the runner merges it into <code>window.env</code>, but no file under <code>servers/nextjs</code> reads <code>ASSETS_BASE_URL</code>; the <code>Window.env</code> type (<code>servers/nextjs/types/global.d.ts:25-32</code>) declares only <code>NEXT_PUBLIC_FAST_API</code>, <code>APP_VERSION</code> and <code>DISABLE_AUTH</code>. If the variable has an effect, it is inside export-core. Do not rely on it from page code without verifying. Note also that the Next.js export path never sets <code>ASSETS_BASE_URL</code>, so in Docker (where <code>NEXT_PUBLIC_FAST_API</code> is unset) that path passes no <code>modifyWindow</code> at all.</p>

servers/nextjs/app/api/export-presentation/route.ts (excerpt)<pre><code>function buildExportDownloadUrl(outPath: string): string {
  const appDataDirectory = process.env.APP_DATA_DIRECTORY?.trim();
  if (!appDataDirectory) {
    throw new Error("APP_DATA_DIRECTORY is required to download exported files.");
  }

  const exportsDirectory = path.join(appDataDirectory, "exports");
  const relativePath = path.relative(exportsDirectory, outPath);
  if (
    !relativePath ||
    relativePath.startsWith("..") ||
    path.isAbsolute(relativePath)
  ) {
    throw new Error("Export finished outside the configured exports directory.");
  }

  return `/api/export-presentation/file?name=${encodeURIComponent(relativePath)}`;
}
</code></pre> <p>The URL carries only a path relative to <code>exports/</code>, never an absolute filesystem path. Step 10.3 shows how the file route re-validates it.</p>

